answer:
Based on the provided context, in its decision, the Central Information Commission or State Information Commission has the power to:

(a) require the public authority to take steps necessary to secure compliance with the Act, including:
    (i) providing access to information in a particular form;
    (ii) appointing a Central Public Information Officer or State Public Information Officer;
    (iii) publishing certain information or categories of information;
    (iv) making necessary changes to record maintenance, management, and destruction practices;
    (v) enhancing training on the right to information for officials;
    (vi) providing an annual report in compliance with section 4(1)(b);
(b) require the public authority to compensate the complainant for any loss or other detriment suffered;
(c) impose any of the penalties provided under the Act;
(d) reject the application.
